WEBVTT

00:12.095 --> 00:13.972
The walls gave the people

00:14.764 --> 00:17.434
a century of peace and security.

00:21.104 --> 00:23.314
The terror of being at their mercy...

00:25.108 --> 00:27.986
and the humiliation of being trapped
became a distant memory.

00:31.406 --> 00:32.407
Until...

00:46.671 --> 00:49.924
The battle for humanity's survival

00:50.759 --> 00:53.386
began the moment
the Titans breached the wall.

00:56.306 --> 01:00.226
After numerous casualties

01:00.685 --> 01:02.771
among soldiers and civilians alike,

01:03.730 --> 01:07.734
it was learned that some Titans
were hiding among the humans.

01:09.152 --> 01:15.241
Finally, humans succeeded in capturing one
of these disguised Titans, Annie Leonhart,

01:16.534 --> 01:20.246
five years after the first wall fell.

01:30.006 --> 01:30.924
Nevertheless...

01:32.300 --> 01:37.931
the next threat to humanity
was already close at hand.

01:52.362 --> 01:53.655
-Hey!
-Look!

02:00.787 --> 02:03.748
-A Titan?
-In the wall?

02:04.290 --> 02:05.375
It can't be!

02:08.628 --> 02:10.255
Your orders, Section Commander?

02:10.588 --> 02:13.550
What? Hold on!

02:14.759 --> 02:17.595
Was that there just by coincidence?

02:18.388 --> 02:21.683
Or does this mean...

02:27.063 --> 02:29.899
-Pastor Nick?
-Whatever you do...

02:31.693 --> 02:35.071
you must keep that Titan
out of the sunlight!

02:37.282 --> 02:38.116
What?

04:15.755 --> 04:19.509
For now, we've covered the Wall Titan
with sheets.

04:20.301 --> 04:22.720
We'll take more proper measures
after sunset.

04:23.471 --> 04:24.305
I see.

04:25.098 --> 04:27.809
What are we supposed to make of this, sir?

04:28.601 --> 04:31.187
I never imagined there would be
Titans in the walls...

04:31.521 --> 04:33.481
No one did.

04:34.732 --> 04:37.902
There were only people who knew
and people who didn't.

04:41.364 --> 04:42.865
What's the deal?

04:43.241 --> 04:47.245
We just fought a Titan here.
Why are they keeping us in the dark?

04:48.454 --> 04:49.289
Business as usual.

04:50.581 --> 04:52.542
But what's most despicable of all

04:54.043 --> 04:59.090
is that there's no "official" reason
why all these people died.

05:02.510 --> 05:03.344
Now then,

05:04.637 --> 05:06.931
it's time for you to talk.

05:08.975 --> 05:11.436
What is this Titan?

05:12.895 --> 05:15.815
What is it doing inside the wall?

05:18.443 --> 05:24.157
And why did you people keep this
a secret all this time?

05:30.079 --> 05:31.789
I have work to do!

05:31.956 --> 05:34.584
My church and its followers
have been devastated!

05:35.001 --> 05:38.296
This is your fault!
I will demand restitution!

05:38.921 --> 05:41.424
Now, let me back down!

05:41.841 --> 05:42.759
Certainly.

05:44.761 --> 05:46.220
Will straight down do?

05:49.515 --> 05:50.892
-Section Commander!
-Stay back.

05:52.101 --> 05:53.311
Enough of this!

05:54.145 --> 05:58.816
Do you people know why we Scouts
have shed so much blood?

05:59.734 --> 06:03.863
To take back our freedom from the Titans!

06:05.156 --> 06:08.576
I was willing to sacrifice my own life
for that cause!

06:10.119 --> 06:14.874
I'm not asking you to talk,
I'm ordering you to. Is that clear?

06:15.541 --> 06:18.086
And if you won't talk,
I'll try the next person.

06:18.795 --> 06:23.549
Your measly life wouldn't make up
for much, anyway!

06:24.509 --> 06:26.761
Let go of me!

06:27.261 --> 06:29.263
Like this? Right now?

06:29.806 --> 06:30.807
Yes!

06:31.182 --> 06:34.268
-Fine, then. Die.
-Section Commander!

06:34.519 --> 06:37.355
Kill me and learn!

06:37.897 --> 06:40.942
We will fulfill our duty, without fail!

06:42.026 --> 06:43.069
So...

06:43.778 --> 06:48.825
let go of me this instant!

06:53.079 --> 06:55.915
Deliver me, O Lord...

07:06.717 --> 07:08.136
Just kidding. I wasn't serious.

07:10.888 --> 07:13.307
Tell me, Pastor Nick...

07:15.476 --> 07:18.521
are all the walls made of Titans?

07:21.274 --> 07:22.150
Section Commander.

07:23.151 --> 07:26.737
Oh, I forgot how this felt.

07:27.738 --> 07:32.910
I haven't felt this way
since my first time outside the walls.

07:36.581 --> 07:37.915
Talk about terrifying...

07:45.673 --> 07:48.301
Hurry! I must inform Commander Erwin!

07:48.634 --> 07:49.635
Hurry!

07:50.052 --> 07:52.430
There are Titans inside Wall Rose!

08:06.068 --> 08:08.571
12 HOURS EARLIER

08:10.072 --> 08:13.326
SOUTH OF WALL SINA

08:16.954 --> 08:20.791
My village isn't far south of here,
you know...

08:21.083 --> 08:23.544
My hometown is close by too.

08:24.128 --> 08:27.798
Damn. Why can't I go visit?

08:29.550 --> 08:31.636
Maybe I'll sneak out at night.

08:32.053 --> 08:37.183
They told me not to come back
until I'm normal.

08:37.767 --> 08:42.104
They told me I was too puny
to be a soldier.

08:42.647 --> 08:47.777
I was smart enough to be one, though.
I was in our class' top ten.

08:47.860 --> 08:50.404
I'm going to make them eat their words.

08:51.113 --> 08:52.114
Conny.

08:52.823 --> 08:54.909
If you're serious, I'll help.

08:54.992 --> 08:56.702
What? How come?

08:57.370 --> 08:59.038
Doesn't it seem strange?

08:59.747 --> 09:01.582
We're on standby
and wearing plain clothes,

09:02.124 --> 09:04.877
and we're not allowed to train
or wear our uniforms.

09:06.796 --> 09:08.089
What's even more suspicious,

09:08.381 --> 09:10.216
everyone else is fully armed.

09:10.841 --> 09:13.970
We're inside the wall,
not on the front lines.

09:14.679 --> 09:16.055
Who are we fighting?

09:16.597 --> 09:20.309
Well, there are bears in the area.

09:20.685 --> 09:22.520
Yes. Bears.

09:22.853 --> 09:24.605
Guns are enough to handle bears.

09:36.450 --> 09:38.828
I hear something!
They sound like footsteps!

09:39.412 --> 09:41.706
-What?
-Seriously, Sasha.

09:42.623 --> 09:44.750
If you're suggesting
there are Titans here,

09:46.043 --> 09:48.921
that would mean Wall Rose has fallen.

09:52.341 --> 09:53.301
Miche?

09:54.051 --> 09:57.638
Tomas! Take three couriers and go!

09:58.055 --> 10:00.141
-What?
-Notify each district!

10:01.976 --> 10:06.105
There are likely no Titans among
the recruits of the 104th Cadet Corps!

10:08.357 --> 10:11.068
Multiple Titans from the south!

10:11.736 --> 10:14.447
Wall Rose has been breached!

10:16.449 --> 10:18.701
It's the truth! I hear footsteps.

10:21.203 --> 10:22.371
Is everyone here?

10:22.955 --> 10:23.873
Nanaba?

10:24.624 --> 10:27.543
Multiple Titans, 500 meters to the south.

10:28.085 --> 10:29.629
They're coming right this way.

10:30.546 --> 10:32.381
There's no time for you to gear up.

10:33.007 --> 10:37.595
Take your horses and evacuate
all nearby homes and settlements.

10:38.095 --> 10:41.140
-Understood?
-From the south?

10:43.100 --> 10:45.269
Has the wall been breached?

10:47.313 --> 10:50.107
Let's get going!
I'm afraid lunch will have to wait.

10:56.864 --> 10:57.698
Miche.

10:59.992 --> 11:03.245
There are nine in that swarm up ahead.

11:07.249 --> 11:09.627
They've broken through Wall Rose.

11:13.923 --> 11:19.053
We never managed to uncover the Titans'
secrets or figure out what they are.

11:19.970 --> 11:21.472
And now the day has come.

11:23.432 --> 11:25.017
Humanity...

11:26.310 --> 11:27.186
has lost.

11:29.730 --> 11:31.816
No. Not yet.

11:34.360 --> 11:38.989
A person only loses
when he stops fighting.

11:40.574 --> 11:44.161
As long as we continue to fight,
we are not beaten!

11:50.501 --> 11:53.087
As soon as the Titans reach the woods,

11:53.462 --> 11:58.050
we'll split into four teams
of recruits and soldiers alike,

11:58.592 --> 12:02.805
and then simultaneously scatter
in each direction!

12:03.305 --> 12:07.143
Avoid combat when possible
and focus on getting the word out!

12:07.435 --> 12:09.937
Is anyone familiar with this region?

12:10.104 --> 12:11.188
Me!

12:11.647 --> 12:13.482
My town's north of here!

12:13.691 --> 12:15.985
I know the lay of the land well!

12:16.735 --> 12:18.237
And so does Conny!

12:20.239 --> 12:22.533
-Conny?
-My village...

12:23.742 --> 12:25.494
My village is to the south,

12:26.078 --> 12:28.122
where the Titans are coming from.

12:29.665 --> 12:32.710
I can take you to nearby villages.
After that,

12:34.003 --> 12:35.629
please let me visit mine.

12:37.965 --> 12:38.966
All right.

12:39.258 --> 12:42.511
-You'll guide the southern team.
-Yes, sir!

12:42.970 --> 12:44.346
I'll come with you, Conny.

12:45.306 --> 12:48.976
The south will be crawling with Titans.
It'll be the most dangerous.

12:49.310 --> 12:53.147
So? I was going to help you
sneak in there anyway, remember?

12:53.647 --> 12:55.691
You coming, Bertholdt?

12:58.861 --> 13:01.113
Of course, I am.

13:04.783 --> 13:06.202
As you may know,

13:06.452 --> 13:09.330
today marks the darkest day
in humanity's history!

13:09.872 --> 13:13.459
If ever there is a time
that humanity needed to give its all,

13:14.084 --> 13:15.127
that time is now!

13:15.336 --> 13:18.047
The Titans have reached the woods!

13:23.719 --> 13:25.095
Scatter!

13:25.429 --> 13:27.765
Ride as fast as you can!

13:39.652 --> 13:40.611
What?

13:40.903 --> 13:42.363
They all started sprinting!

13:42.780 --> 13:44.448
They're going to catch up!

13:46.450 --> 13:47.535
Gerger!

13:48.994 --> 13:52.289
-Take charge of the southern team!
-Sir?

13:54.333 --> 13:56.085
Understood.

13:56.794 --> 13:58.796
He's using himself as bait?

13:59.046 --> 14:03.676
-He won't survive! I'll help!
-No! We can't spare anyone else!

14:04.385 --> 14:05.761
Have faith in him!

14:06.345 --> 14:08.973
His skill is second only to Captain Levi!

14:09.682 --> 14:11.600
He'll make it back alive!

14:42.548 --> 14:43.632
Oh, Eren.

14:44.425 --> 14:46.552
Did you get into another fight?

14:47.303 --> 14:49.555
Those jerks started it!

14:50.180 --> 14:51.473
They made fun of me!

14:51.724 --> 14:56.020
So, I assume Mikasa had to come
to your rescue again?

14:57.229 --> 14:58.355
Thanks.

15:03.819 --> 15:04.778
Eren.

15:04.987 --> 15:07.740
No matter how cruel someone is
or how much you hate them,

15:08.032 --> 15:10.117
you can't always charge at them head-on!

15:12.286 --> 15:13.537
You're a man!

15:13.996 --> 15:16.957
Show some self-discipline!
You need to be there for Mikasa, too!

16:05.631 --> 16:06.632
That's...

16:07.633 --> 16:08.634
It fell.

16:10.386 --> 16:12.763
You must be tired. Go get some sleep.

16:14.181 --> 16:16.141
Sorry. I'm fine.

16:17.393 --> 16:19.061
That thing's seen better days.

16:21.397 --> 16:24.316
I'll get you a new one
if I see any in our supplies.

16:31.365 --> 16:32.658
Eren! Mikasa!

16:33.492 --> 16:34.743
This is bad!

16:35.285 --> 16:36.370
The Titans!

16:36.787 --> 16:38.122
They're inside Wall Rose!

16:45.504 --> 16:48.674
Those damn Titans never give us a break.

16:51.010 --> 16:51.969
Can you go?

16:53.095 --> 16:54.596
It's not like there's a choice.

16:55.764 --> 16:59.768
It was wise to have
Section Commander Miche watch the 104th.

17:00.310 --> 17:02.271
I believe he can handle the situation.

17:03.313 --> 17:04.148
Yes.

17:05.733 --> 17:07.067
Let's hope so.

17:24.334 --> 17:25.919
Four left.

17:32.384 --> 17:34.511
No, it's time to go.

17:35.304 --> 17:37.306
I've bought enough time.

17:46.690 --> 17:47.608
Still...

17:48.442 --> 17:50.694
I'm concerned about that Abnormal.

17:51.737 --> 17:53.072
It's different.

17:53.864 --> 17:55.991
It looks over 17 meters tall.

17:57.034 --> 17:58.243
It's huge.

17:58.702 --> 18:02.748
And I've never seen
a Titan covered in fur before.

18:03.832 --> 18:07.878
It's just walking around
instead of coming for me.

18:08.212 --> 18:10.506
It's an Abnormal, but...

18:13.258 --> 18:15.219
Great! You're back!

18:15.844 --> 18:18.472
I won't need to hold out until nightfall.

18:26.230 --> 18:28.398
It went for the horse?

18:29.650 --> 18:30.609
You can't be serious!

18:52.339 --> 18:53.215
Wait.

19:14.236 --> 19:19.241
What? Didn't I just say to wait?

19:39.386 --> 19:42.306
What is that weapon called?

19:47.519 --> 19:50.355
That thing on your waist
that flies around.

20:02.784 --> 20:05.704
I'm certain we speak the same language.

20:06.121 --> 20:08.790
Perhaps you're simply too frightened.

20:09.791 --> 20:12.628
Oh, I see you use swords too.

20:13.378 --> 20:17.257
I guess that means you know
we reside in the nape.

20:17.841 --> 20:21.762
Oh, well. I'll just take it back with me.

20:46.578 --> 20:51.458
A person only loses
when he stops fighting.

20:56.588 --> 20:58.840
As long as we continue to fight,

21:00.592 --> 21:02.761
we are not beaten!

21:10.143 --> 21:12.271
You can move now.

21:17.859 --> 21:22.114
No!

21:22.239 --> 21:26.618
Stop! Don't! No!

21:30.038 --> 21:32.624
So you can speak.

21:37.587 --> 21:41.466
I must say, what a clever idea.

21:44.594 --> 21:47.472
No!

21:47.806 --> 21:51.768
Stop! No!

23:25.112 --> 23:28.365
Titans have suddenly appeared
inside Wall Rose.

23:29.616 --> 23:31.451
The recruits from the 104th Cadet Corps

23:31.868 --> 23:34.704
scatter across the land
to spread the news.

23:35.872 --> 23:39.417
Meanwhile, Eren and the others
head to their rescue.

23:41.670 --> 23:47.759
And after returning to her hometown,
Sasha comes face-to-face with her past.

23:49.136 --> 23:52.389
Next episode, "I'm Home."
